  "ownership_contract": [
    "MapMetadataBase is private and sealed to precisely BaseIndexedMapStorage and BaseDoubleMapStorage. Its associated observations contain owned numeric metadata; no public generic unsafe API or arbitrary observer callback exists.",
    "MapTopology is not Clone, exposes no Arc constructor/access and cannot be recovered from an observer. Unique owner edit requires &mut and locks; owner read is shared and observers never mutate.",
    "Exchange swaps the actual bases inside their original stable Arc identities under both locks. Distinct unique owners cannot share a state.",
    "Only the metadata state has the shared unsafe Send/Sync implementation. Typed owner and range payload/hasher bounds, covariance, Unpin and unwind bounds are unchanged.",
    "Snapshots lock and copy metadata, allocator/table addresses and slot identities without dereferencing nodes. This includes native Clear phases with transient freed-head identities. User hash/equal/clone/drop callbacks remain outside edit locks.",
    "Owner destruction drains payloads and empties tables before its handle drops. Independent observers may survive and release the emptied metadata allocation on a different thread, including when payloads were non-Send."
  ],
